    {
      "id": 391606,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "A Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability was found on TikTok incentive endpoint via x parameter, due to the reflection of user-supplied data without appropriate HTML escaping or output encoding. As a result, a JavaScript payload could be injected into the affected endpoint causing it to be executed within the context of a user's browser. We thank @ashrafabdelrazik for reporting this to our team. ",
